<title>CHINA: Lehman appoints head of S.E. Asian equity trade.</title>
<headline>Lehman appoints head of S.E. Asian equity trade.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said on Wednesday it has hired Sching Lin to run its Hong Kong based South East Asian equity trading businesses.</p>
<p>Lin was formerly a director in the equity capital markets division at Salomon Brothers in Hong Kong, the investment bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Lin reports directly to Richard Lemmerman, head of Asian equities, based in Tokyo, it said.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers involves in corporate and municipal finance and advisory services and in securities sales, trading and research businesses. -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
